WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.302
- President Trump,
and I was there,

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.536
I was literally negotiating

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:05.538
between the White
House and Congress.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.107
The president had me here

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:08.441
and then I would go
across the street

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:09.943
and speak to Speaker Pelosi.

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:11.644
Speaker Pelosi would tell me
to go back to the White House.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:13.480
So I was negotiating
between the White House

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.481
and Congress on this.

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:15.715
There was a great deal.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.617
President Trump
even surprised me

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:18.918
with the number of Dreamers.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:20.920
He increased it times two.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.923
He went from 800,000 to
1.6 million dreamers.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:26.126
"Pastor Sam, we're
gonna give Dreamers

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:28.828
a pathway to citizenship
as long as I get my wall

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:33.333 align:start size:97% position:3%
and protect the border and
stop all illegal immigration."

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.368 align:start position:0%
And I went back to the speaker,
we negotiated something.

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:36.903 align:start size:81% position:19%
And then Chuck
Schumer came along

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:39.739
and said, "We're not gonna
give President Trump a win."

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:41.508
Do your due diligence on this,

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:43.309
it's been extensively covered.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:45.845
(gentle music)

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:52.318 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
- I'm Dave Rubin and joining
me today is the president

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:54.954 line:0%
of the National Christian
Leadership Conference,

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:57.690 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
as well as the
author of "Be Light."

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.059
Reverend Samuel Rodriguez,

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.860
welcome to "The Rubin Report."

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Thank you for having me.
- I'm glad to have you

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:06.232
because there's obviously a
lot going on in your world.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:11.204 align:start position:0%
Not only is it just past
Easter and the Passover season,

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.605 align:start size:84% position:16%
but obviously there's
a ton going on

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.507
on the immigration front.

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:17.143 align:start position:0%
And many of the things that
I've been seeing you talk about,

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.745
mostly on Fox lately,
are a lot of the things

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:19.979
that I talk about on this show.

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.815 align:start size:84% position:16%
And you made some
sense on cable news,

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:24.184 align:start size:84% position:16%
that's a pretty rare
thing these days,

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.385 align:start size:81% position:19%
so I thought I
could have you on.

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:26.886 align:start size:84% position:16%
For the people that
don't know you,

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:29.456
can you give me a little bit
about your backstory first

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:31.958 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then we'll move
into the current days?

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.495 line:0%
- Yeah, I'm a kid from
Bethlehem, Pennsylvania,

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:38.198 line:0%
hence Bethlehem, I have
a messianic complex.

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:41.968
My dad was a Mack truck worker.

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.303
My mom was a homemaker.

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:45.605
I graduated from
Lehigh University.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.174
I was raised in an
evangelical home.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.310
My parents are not preachers.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:53.046
I'm a faith and science guy.

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:56.116
Ronald Reagan inspired the
living daylights out of me

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.752
and just prompted
this commitment

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.888 align:start size:84% position:16%
to changing America
and the world

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:05.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
with a value system that's
Judeo-Christian based,

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:07.393 align:start size:84% position:16%
but this radical
idea of God over man

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:08.962
and man over government.

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.363
And so that's what we do.

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:12.665 align:start size:97% position:3%
My commitment is to reconcile
Billy Graham's message

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:13.933
of Dr. King's March.

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:16.002
I call it the Lamb's
Agenda, it's doable.

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:18.671 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So you said a faith
and science guy.

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:21.774 align:start size:88% position:13%
I know my more skeptical
audience members,

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.443
their antennas just went off.

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:26.179 align:start size:84% position:16%
What does a faith
and science guy mean?

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:27.814 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, I'm an
evangelical trekkie.

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:29.382
So I'm a faith and science guy.

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:32.252 align:start size:84% position:16%
I believe that science
is the wonderful

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:36.656 align:start size:97% position:3%
horizontal expression of
the reality of a living God.

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:42.028
I follow everything
from quantum physics.

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:44.097
My encounter with God
at the highest level

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:46.366 align:start size:84% position:16%
took place in my
undergraduate studies

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:49.169
at Penn State University in
a quantum physics course.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.705
So I did not come
through the normal,

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:56.109 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know watching a television
Christian broadcast.

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:56.943 align:start size:84% position:16%
That did not happen.
- Can you explain

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:57.911
that a little further?

00:02:57.911 --> 00:02:58.578
That's pretty interesting.

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah, math and
science, it blew me away.

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:04.884
The Newtonian laws, Leipzig,

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:07.954
the ever-increasing
reality of a universe

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:12.458
that continues to expand,
the beauty of the Big Bang,

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:14.928
the intricacies of the minerals

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:17.630 align:start size:84% position:16%
that are out there in
the universe, likewise
on this planet,

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:20.400 align:start size:97% position:3%
likewise in your bloodstream,
in my bloodstream,

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.337
the mathematical probability
of that happening by chance,

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:27.006 align:start size:81% position:19%
it requires you
to have more faith

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:31.211 align:start size:88% position:13%
not to believe in a
designer, and I'm sorry,

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:35.114 align:start size:97% position:3%
I don't have that crazy
cuckoo for cocoa puff faith.

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:36.416
It does require you
to have more faith

00:03:36.416 --> 00:03:39.018 align:start size:84% position:16%
to believe this
happened by chance.

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:42.255 align:start size:88% position:13%
And just the math and
the science all adds up.

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:44.791
I'm a student of a guy
named Francis Collins

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:49.295
who oversees the National
Health Institute right now.

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:51.364
And he has been for a
number of presidents,

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:53.733
for Obama and Trump.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:56.769 align:start size:88% position:13%
So again, he discovered
to a great degree,

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:59.906
unpack, unpack better
yet, the human genome,

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:01.641
and he is a believer.

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:03.943
So again, I don't
create a dichotomy

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.678
between faith and science.

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:06.679
I think it's beautiful.

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:09.249
It's one metanarrative stream

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:13.686
that speaks to a wonderful
architect, a designer, a God.

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:15.421
- Do you think that one
of our biggest problems

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:19.158 align:start size:88% position:13%
discussing this is that
too many people do,

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:21.127
"Oh, it's just either/or,

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:23.129
you're either a believer in God

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:24.864
or you're a believer in science.

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:26.199
These things can't touch."

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:30.536
- Right, that is
a false dichotomy.

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:33.806 align:start position:0%
Because I am a believer in
God, I'm a believer in science.

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:36.009
Absolutely.

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.310 align:start size:84% position:16%
And because I'm a
believer in science,

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:38.478
I'm a believer in God.

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:41.247
It's one continual stream.

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:43.716
I think we suffer from
cognitive dissonance.

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:47.420 align:start size:97% position:3%
We're lacking the sort of
cerebral bandwidth and Wi-Fi

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.422
to really look at
the big picture.

00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:51.758 align:start size:84% position:16%
And if we do adhere
to, succumb to,

00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:55.295
or acquiesce to the
idea of a designer,

00:04:55.295 --> 00:05:00.266
then everything else becomes
a little bit more palpable.

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:04.237
And if that designer has
a plan for the universe,

00:05:04.237 --> 00:05:06.639
does he have a design and a
plan for individual lives?

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:08.341 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then it becomes
more personal.

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:10.576
And that's where I come in
as a pastor and a preacher

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:13.112
and dissect that and bring
it about every single Sunday.

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:16.282
- So speaking of your
job as a preacher,

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:19.385
in this last year where we've
had lockdowns and pandemic

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:21.421
and people outta work
and all of that stuff,

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:22.889
have you noticed people looking

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:26.125 align:start position:0%
for something different
spiritually or from the church?

00:05:28.094 --> 00:05:29.562 align:start size:84% position:16%
- You know what,
Dave, you would assume

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:34.100 align:start size:97% position:3%
that a global pandemic would
catapult the measurement

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:37.337
or the metric of
agnosticism, right?

00:05:37.337 --> 00:05:39.072
Just from a logical continuum.

00:05:39.072 --> 00:05:40.973 align:start size:84% position:16%
If there's a God,
how could he permit?

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:44.243 align:start size:88% position:13%
It is the quintessential
query, right?

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:46.479
If there's a God, why does
he permit evil to happen,

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:48.014
that sort of thing.

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:51.017
So a global pandemic, over
500,000 deaths in America,

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:53.453
there can't be.

00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:54.587
Well, guess what?

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:55.855
Every single survey,

00:05:55.855 --> 00:05:58.291
including one I just
read four days ago,

00:05:58.291 --> 00:06:01.794
the level of spiritual hunger
has increased exponentially.

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:05.264 align:start size:97% position:3%
Now, I'm not saying
explore organized religion.

00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:07.667
I'm saying the level
of spiritual hunger

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:10.036
has increased exponentially.

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:14.273
So, people are hungry for
a relationship with God,

00:06:14.273 --> 00:06:18.411 align:start position:0%
for greater spirituality,
spiritual awakening, awareness.

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:20.246
So, that's where we come in.

00:06:20.246 --> 00:06:21.981
And that's why I fought back

00:06:21.981 --> 00:06:24.150 align:start size:84% position:16%
when Governor Newsom
in California,

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.519
in our collective state,
you are a part of that-

00:06:26.519 --> 00:06:29.922 align:start size:97% position:3%
- You are in California,
you are in California, yeah.

00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:32.091 align:start size:88% position:13%
I didn't wanna out you,
you outed yourself.

00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:34.594
- I outed myself.

00:06:34.594 --> 00:06:37.997
When when he deemed casinos
and liquor stores essential,

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:42.201
but churches and synagogues
not, are you kidding me?

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:46.038 align:start size:88% position:13%
Guess who gets the
call for health issues?

00:06:46.038 --> 00:06:47.507
We do.

00:06:47.507 --> 00:06:49.709
When young men and
women right now,

00:06:49.709 --> 00:06:52.512 align:start size:97% position:3%
greater numbers in California
as it pertains to God,

00:06:52.512 --> 00:06:55.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's unfortunate, the
suicide rate, drug abuse,

00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:59.118 align:start size:97% position:3%
alcoholism, depression, we've
never seen these numbers.

00:06:59.118 --> 00:07:00.586
Guess who they call?

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:02.488
They don't call the guy
in the liquor store.

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:06.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
So Jack Daniels should
not trump Moses and Jesus.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:10.196 align:start position:0%
It's just illogical, but
that's what Governor Newsom did

00:07:10.196 --> 00:07:13.433
while he was having dinner
at "The French Laundry,"

00:07:13.433 --> 00:07:15.168 align:start size:81% position:19%
and that's another
story perhaps.

00:07:15.168 --> 00:07:17.103
- My audience knows
that story well,

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:19.572
so fear not, we don't have
to dive too much into that.

00:07:19.572 --> 00:07:21.707 align:start size:84% position:16%
But you mentioned sort
of the role of God,

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:24.444
of government, of man,
all of those things.

00:07:24.444 --> 00:07:26.646 align:start size:88% position:13%
You've been able to
piece something together

00:07:26.646 --> 00:07:27.914
that's pretty holistic

00:07:27.914 --> 00:07:30.783
that sort of forms your
political views as well,

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:31.617
it sounds like.

00:07:32.885 --> 00:07:35.154
- God over man, man
over government,

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:36.456
that's the pecking order.

00:07:36.456 --> 00:07:39.625 align:start position:0%
That's American exceptionalism,
that right there.

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:41.627
God over man, man
over government.

00:07:41.627 --> 00:07:44.063
And when government grows,

00:07:44.063 --> 00:07:46.232
it's gonna sound a
little bit naive,

00:07:46.232 --> 00:07:49.135
or, you know, here it
is, government grows,

00:07:49.135 --> 00:07:52.271
it pushes man and
God outta the way.

00:07:52.271 --> 00:07:55.107 align:start size:84% position:16%
This uber dependency
on government

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:58.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this unbelievable
obsession with Uncle Sam,

00:07:58.711 --> 00:08:01.047
it's not part of the ethos
of our founding fathers.

00:08:01.047 --> 00:08:04.417 align:start size:97% position:3%
It isn't, it's
anti-American, it really is.

00:08:04.417 --> 00:08:07.119
This obsession with government,

00:08:07.119 --> 00:08:10.656 align:start size:97% position:3%
instead of our God-ordained
giftings and abilities,

00:08:10.656 --> 00:08:12.658
Uncle Sam is an uncle.

00:08:12.658 --> 00:08:14.560
He'll never be our
Heavenly father.

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:16.195
He's just an uncle.

00:08:16.195 --> 00:08:17.663
So, we respect the uncle,

00:08:17.663 --> 00:08:21.167 align:start size:97% position:3%
unless the uncle gets
drunk in that family party.

00:08:21.167 --> 00:08:25.238
We respect the uncle,
but we worship God.

00:08:25.238 --> 00:08:27.673
And right now, and even
the recent proposals

00:08:27.673 --> 00:08:29.175
from the Biden administration,

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:33.746
not just the 1.9 trillion, but
now the infrastructure bill,

00:08:33.746 --> 00:08:38.384 align:start size:97% position:3%
all of this, this unbridled
growth of government,

00:08:38.384 --> 00:08:41.921 align:start position:0%
ladies and gentlemen,
government is becoming our God.

00:08:41.921 --> 00:08:46.192 align:start size:97% position:3%
Well, I'm pretty sure-
- And we are what we tolerate.

00:08:46.192 --> 00:08:47.193
So we're tolerating.

00:08:47.193 --> 00:08:48.394
- Yeah, and I'm pretty sure

00:08:48.394 --> 00:08:50.296 align:start size:81% position:19%
the uncle is drunk
at the moment.

00:08:50.296 --> 00:08:53.232
He's drunk and he's spending
a lot of other people's money.

00:08:53.232 --> 00:08:56.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you view that
obsession with government

00:08:56.802 --> 00:08:59.505
as just the next
step down the road

00:08:59.505 --> 00:09:01.007
because of the God-shaped hole?

00:09:01.007 --> 00:09:03.943
That if basically you
are not a believer,

00:09:03.943 --> 00:09:05.311
you gotta believe in something,

00:09:05.311 --> 00:09:07.547 align:start size:88% position:13%
and then government just
kind of fills it in?

00:09:10.049 --> 00:09:12.451
- Do we have measurable elements

00:09:12.451 --> 00:09:14.053
that we can dissect historically

00:09:14.053 --> 00:09:16.489
so it's not hype and it's
not rhetorical exuberance?

00:09:16.489 --> 00:09:17.757
Can we measure it?

00:09:17.757 --> 00:09:19.559
Let's measure it.

00:09:19.559 --> 00:09:22.628 align:start size:88% position:13%
Right after World War
II, 76% of all Americans

00:09:22.628 --> 00:09:25.765
attended a church
or synagogue, 76%.

00:09:25.765 --> 00:09:28.100 align:start size:97% position:3%
That number according to last
week's survey from Gallup

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:30.803
is now 48% for the first time.

00:09:30.803 --> 00:09:32.071
What does this mean?

00:09:32.071 --> 00:09:33.372
Let's not forget what
we were fighting back

00:09:33.372 --> 00:09:35.708
in the '40s and '50s, communism,

00:09:35.708 --> 00:09:38.945
this idea of unbridled
government being God,

00:09:38.945 --> 00:09:41.647
stemming out of the
USSR, through China,

00:09:41.647 --> 00:09:42.915
all around the world.

00:09:42.915 --> 00:09:44.717
Here it is, it's 2021.

00:09:45.785 --> 00:09:47.153
Government is growing.

00:09:47.153 --> 00:09:50.289
God, God and meaning
the belief in God,

00:09:50.289 --> 00:09:52.224
is decreasing in America.

00:09:52.224 --> 00:09:53.993
It's directly parallel.

00:09:53.993 --> 00:09:55.661
It's directly proportional.

00:09:55.661 --> 00:09:57.730
The more we get away from God,

00:09:57.730 --> 00:10:00.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
the more government plays
a role in our lives.

00:10:00.733 --> 00:10:03.069 line:0%
I'm telling you, it's
replacement theology.

00:10:03.069 --> 00:10:05.037 line:0%
It's not like we're
doing away with God

00:10:05.037 --> 00:10:06.472 line:0%
and then there's
this great vacuum.

00:10:06.472 --> 00:10:08.741 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
There is spiritual hunger
and there's hunger,

00:10:08.741 --> 00:10:11.110 align:start size:97% position:3%
this is gonna seem a
little bit difficult for me

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:16.115
as a viral view, this
issue of dependency.

00:10:17.283 --> 00:10:19.251 align:start size:84% position:16%
So who do we depend
on, God or government?

00:10:19.251 --> 00:10:22.121
