continual conversation with God,

00:37:38.589 --> 00:37:43.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
with my thoughts to prove,
to test my ideology,

00:37:43.060 --> 00:37:44.929
my belief system.

00:37:44.929 --> 00:37:46.464
I think it's beautiful.

00:37:46.464 --> 00:37:49.867
And I don't think God is ever
afraid of our questions, ever.

00:37:49.867 --> 00:37:53.904 align:start position:0%
I think we have a God who
welcomes queries and questions.

00:37:53.904 --> 00:37:55.873
I love it, I love it, I love it.

00:37:55.873 --> 00:37:57.308
I just absolutely love it.

00:37:57.308 --> 00:38:01.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hey, Adam and Eve,
Genesis, God turns around

00:38:01.612 --> 00:38:05.916
and says after the fall,
"Hey, Adam, where are you?"

00:38:05.916 --> 00:38:09.353 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like he didn't know, right?
(Dave chuckling)

00:38:09.353 --> 00:38:11.756 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's just a question
of find yourself.

00:38:11.756 --> 00:38:13.824
Do you know where
you really are,

00:38:13.824 --> 00:38:18.229 align:start size:97% position:3%
really, in life, with me,
with purpose, where are you?

00:38:18.229 --> 00:38:19.263
So I love questions.

00:38:19.263 --> 00:38:21.032
Doubts don't bother me.

00:38:21.032 --> 00:38:26.037
I welcome them, as long as they
don't put a lid on my faith.

00:38:27.238 --> 00:38:29.407
- I'm curious, did
you track the rise

00:38:29.407 --> 00:38:30.775
